Hello,

I have proposed a BoF session for ELCE 2017 titled "Bash the kernel 
maintainers" which has been accepted.

The purpose of the session is to gather pain points, suggestions and any other 
kind of feedback regarding the kernel maintenance process from developers who 
do not attend the Kernel Summit and/or who usually stay silent due to the 
false idea that the voice of occasional developers doesn't matter.

The session is scheduled for Monday October the 23rd (https://
osseu17.sched.com/event/ByYK/bash-the-kernel-maintainers-laurent-pinchart-
ideas-on-board). My plan is to submit an article with LWN.net with the 
gathered feedback. If there is sufficient interest I can also provide a brief 
readout during the maintainers summit.

